+      "id": "F12",
+      "lesson": 3,
+      "field": "content_html",
+      "severity": "HIGH",
+      "claim": "Workers must use atmospheric monitoring equipment to test air quality before entering and while working",
+      "truth": "Testing and monitoring are required where the risk assessment identifies an unsafe or potentially changing atmosphere. The competent person defines the testing and monitoring needed in the safe system of work.",
+      "evidence": "HSE, Safe work in confined spaces, paras 89–92",
+      "verdict": "FIX"
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "F13",
+      "lesson": 3,
+      "field": "content_html",
+      "severity": "HIGH",
+      "claim": "a trained attendant must remain outside the space at all times",
+      "truth": "Suitable rescue arrangements must be in place before entry. They depend on the risk assessment; guidance says someone should normally attend outside to communicate, raise the alarm and take charge of rescue, rather than imposing that exact arrangement in every case.",
+      "evidence": "spec 1.8.6; HSE, Safe work in confined spaces; HSE, Health and safety in construction HSG150",
+      "verdict": "FIX"
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "F14",
+      "lesson": 1,
+      "field": "exam_tip_html",
+      "severity": "MEDIUM",
+      "claim": "writing \"a qualified person\" alone is not specific enough to earn the mark",
+      "truth": "The specification names Gas Safe as an example of an accreditation but does not prescribe mark-credit rules for this wording. Either retain this as house guidance without a mark claim, or support it with the relevant published mark scheme.",
+      "evidence": "spec 4.1; spec 1.8.5",
+      "verdict": "ADJUDICATE"
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "F15",
+      "lesson": 2,
+      "field": "exam_tip_html",
+      "severity": "MEDIUM",
+      "claim": "do not write \"health and safety law\" alone, as this is too vague to earn the mark",
+      "truth": "The specification gives the assessment format and subject content but no mark-credit rule for this wording. Either recast the advice as a study recommendation or support it with the relevant published mark scheme.",
+      "evidence": "spec 4.1; spec 1.8.3",
+      "verdict": "ADJUDICATE"
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "F16",
+      "lesson": 3,
+      "field": "exam_tip_html",
+      "severity": "MEDIUM",
+      "claim": "examiners frequently award marks for naming the specific access methods",
+      "truth": "The specification requires learners to understand appropriate methods of access but does not state a frequency or mark award for naming them. Either recast this as study advice or support it with the relevant published mark scheme.",
+      "evidence": "spec 1.8.6; spec 4.1",
+      "verdict": "ADJUDICATE"
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "F17",
+      "lesson": 3,
+      "field": "content_html",
+      "severity": "MEDIUM",
+      "claim": "An untrained bystander ... will almost certainly be overcome themselves ... the majority of the victims were would-be rescuers.",
+      "truth": "HSE guidance supports the risk of a second casualty and says the second person is often a would-be rescuer, but the fetched sources do not support the probability claims. Either qualify them to ‘may’ and ‘often’, or provide a source for the statistics.",
+      "evidence": "HSE, Managing confined spaces on farms; HSE, Health and safety in construction HSG150",
+      "verdict": "ADJUDICATE"
+    }
+  ],
+  "lessons_clean": [],
+  "summary": "Verified corrections address legal scope, statutory duties, accreditation, isolation and confined-space safety. Four exam or probability claims need an editorial decision because the accessible specification and sources do not support their absolute wording."
+}

