+      "field": "content_html",
+      "severity": "MEDIUM",
+      "claim": "The Health and Safety at Work Act (1974) is the cornerstone of workplace safety law in the UK.",
+      "truth": "The 1974 Act is the main workplace safety law in Great Britain. It does not extend to Northern Ireland, where the Health and Safety at Work (Northern Ireland) Order 1978 is the primary legislation.",
+      "evidence": "spec 1.8.3 footnote 4; legislation.gov.uk, Health and Safety at Work etc. Act 1974 s84; nidirect, Employers’ health and safety responsibilities",
+      "verdict": "FIX"
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "F6",
+      "lesson": 2,
+      "field": "content_html",
+      "severity": "HIGH",
+      "claim": "Under this Act, employers in construction are legally required to prepare risk assessments",
